[{:seon.task/name "the-shipped-task-files-load"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists (merged): `seon.task-files-test/the-shipped-task-files-load` loads resources/seon/tasks into a test branch with `seon.task/load-tx` and expects no error. Before, an unescaped double quote inside one plan string made `(my.root/load-tasks! sys dir)` answer :seon.task/refused (\"not readable EDN: Map literal must contain an even number of forms\") and no task file loaded, unseen because no test read the shipped directory. An error names the file; its line (from the reader's ex-data) would help."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.task-files-test/the-shipped-task-files-load}}
 {:seon.task/name "an-agent-reads-its-task-as-main-holds-it"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `my.task/current` reads the agent's task on its own branch (`seon.agent/db`), forked before the run was written, so it reads its execution as held while main reads running. Correct: the execution an agent reads is main's at its turn's basis, or the render says which db it read."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.task-test/an-agent-reads-its-task-running}}
 {:seon.task/name "merged-work-leaves-the-task-files"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: a task's state is derived from its runs on main (`seon.reconcile/task-state`), so work a Seon agent merges reads `:merged`. Work a worktree session merges into main has no run, and its entry in `resources/seon/tasks/` reads the same before and after: of the shipped tasks, dozens are merged work that loads as open (`seon.task/the-shipped-task-files-load` loads them all). What correct looks like (simplest, no new key): the merge that merges a task's work removes its entry from the task file in the same commit; git keeps the plan and its proofs stay in test/. A task still worked by Seon agents keeps its derived state. Proposed, not decided: root rules before it is built (docs/tasks.md#where-a-tasks-state-lives). Deletes: the merged entries now in the files."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.task-files-test/no-shipped-task-is-merged-work}}
 {:seon.task/name "design-writes-the-implement-steps-proofs"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `my.task/update!` edits only this agent's own :seon.task/plan or :seon.task/instructions, and `seon.merge/carried-platform-attrs` carries only those two, so the proofs a design step writes for implement reach main only as plan text. Reproduction: a staged request with no proofs (`seon.template/stages`); design writes red deftests and rewrites its plan; implement is refused :no-proofs by `seon.reconcile/done-explain` (recorded in task seon.template/a-request-is-one-linked-transaction). Cause: no function edits another task's members, and proofs are not carried. Correct (DESIGN-tasks §5.2, prototyped): ``my.task/edit!`` (id f & args: clojure.core/update on any authored member of any task, written on the branch), and :seon.task/proofs among what `seon.task/carry-tx` carries. Deletes: `my.task/update!`."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.task-test/edit-writes-another-tasks-proofs seon.reconcile-test/implement-holds-the-proofs-design-wrote}}]
